<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip II of France</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1165–1223</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Philip Augustus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, known as Philip Augustus, was king of France from 1180 to 1223. He conquered Normandy, Anjou, Maine and Poitou from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1204 and won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bouvines">Battle of Bouvines</a> in 1214, breaking the Angevin Empire. His reign greatly enlarged the royal domain and made the Capetian monarchy the strongest power in France.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france.jpg" alt="Philip II of France" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sceau_de_Philippe_Auguste._-_Archives_Nationales_-_SC-D157.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
